{
  "category": "reflection-stories",
  "title": "Some Things Don’t Leave",
  "slug": "some-things-dont-leave",
  "publishedAt": "2026-05-12T10:00:00.000Z",
  "draft": false,
  "excerpt": "Some people don’t disappear. They just become harder to reach. And the hardest part is not losing someone — it’s realizing they’re still there, just not fully with you anymore.",
  "body": {
    "type": "root",
    "children": [
      {
        "type": "p",
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "He never really raised his voice."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "p",
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Even when he was upset, everything stayed controlled, quiet, contained."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "p",
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "At first, she thought that meant he was calm. Safe."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "p",
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "But over time, she started noticing something harder to name."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "p",
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The things he didn’t say began to fill the space between them."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "p",
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "One evening, after an argument that never fully became an argument — no shouting, just silence — she said:"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "p",
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "“I feel like you leave before you actually leave.”"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "p",
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "He looked at her for a long moment."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "p",
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "And then said quietly,"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "p",
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "“I don’t leave. I just don’t know how to stay fully here.”"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "p",
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "That stayed with her."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "p",
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Because she realized something she hadn’t been able to see before:"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "p",
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Some people don’t disappear."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "p",
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "They just become harder to reach."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "p",
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "And the hardest part is not losing someone."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "p",
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "It’s realizing they’re still there…"
          },
          {
            "type": "break",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ""
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "just not fully with you anymore."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
